      "body": "<!-- \u26a0\ufe0f\u26a0\ufe0f Do Not Delete This! bug_report_template \u26a0\ufe0f\u26a0\ufe0f -->\r\n<!-- Please read our Rules of Conduct: https://opensource.microsoft.com/codeofconduct/ -->\r\n<!-- \ud83d\udd6e Read our guide about submitting issues: https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/Submitting-Bugs-and-Suggestions -->\r\n<!-- \ud83d\udd0e Search existing issues to avoid creating duplicates. -->\r\n<!-- \ud83e\uddea Test using the latest Insiders build to see if your issue has already been fixed: https://code.visualstudio.com/insiders/ -->\r\n<!-- \ud83d\udca1 Instead of creating your report here, use 'Report Issue' from the 'Help' menu in VS Code to pre-fill useful information. -->\r\n<!-- \ud83d\udd27 Launch with `code --disable-extensions` to check. -->\r\nDoes this issue occur when all extensions are disabled?: Yes\r\n\r\n<!-- \ud83e\ude93 If you answered No above, use 'Help: Start Extension Bisect' from Command Palette to try to identify the cause. -->\r\n<!-- \ud83d\udce3 Issues caused by an extension need to be reported directly to the extension publisher. The 'Help > Report Issue' dialog can assist with this. -->\r\n- VS Code Version: \r\n```\r\nVersion: 1.77.0 (Universal)\r\nCommit: 7f329fe6c66b0f86ae1574c2911b681ad5a45d63\r\nDate: 2023-03-29T09:57:11.797Z (2 days ago)\r\nElectron: 19.1.11\r\nChromium: 102.0.5005.196\r\nNode.js: 16.14.2\r\nV8: 10.2.154.26-electron.0\r\nOS: Darwin x64 21.2.0\r\nSandboxed: No\r\n```\r\n- OS Version: Mac OS Monteray 12.1 (21C52)\r\n\r\nSteps to Reproduce using my personal layout:\r\n\r\n1. Clone keyboard layout https://github.com/Kalhama/unofficial-finnish-dvorak\r\n2. Install keyboard bundle as global as not all applications seem to respect layouts installed only for the user.\r\n3. Optional: Reboot computer to ensure that layout is loaded properly\r\n4. Switch to the custom layout\r\n5. Try using hotkeys such as `cmd + c, cmd + v`. In other applications (including Electron) layout works as intended, but vscode does'n seem to respect the layout change when modifier key cmd is pressed down.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots of the layout ##\r\nno modifiers pressed:\r\n<img width=\"1303\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/19395917/229140427-31462687-24e0-4427-b511-5c6331c84248.png\">\r\n\r\ncmd modifier pressed:\r\n<img width=\"1303\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/19395917/229140462-cc23fe7a-b4b6-4cab-9121-d127440258c8.png\">\r\n\r\n## More information regarding the matter ##\r\nVScode seems to rely quite heavily keycode when managing hotkeys even though it's [deprecated](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/KeyboardEvent/keyCode) . Keycodes don't change when layout index is changed. Better solution would be to use key, as webkit already manages the layouts properly.\r\n\r\nOther electron apps seem to work this way as I haven't encountered issues with them (as long as layout is installed globally). Tested Discord, Whatsapp, Telegram, Spotify...\r\n\r\n## Workarounds ##\r\nRemap every hotkey in vscode, possible to do via script.",
